## Bug

**Root cause:** \proxy.ts\ uses hostname-based routing to distinguish between app, API, and public (marketing) domains. The \isPublicDomain\ flag is true when the hostname does **not** start with \^Gpp.\ or \^Gpi.\.

In CI/E2E, the server runs on \127.0.0.1\ which matches neither prefix — so \isPublicDomain = true\. The proxy then:
1. Rewrites \/\ → \/landing\ (line 99)
2. Redirects \/landing\ → \/\ (line 104)

This creates an infinite redirect loop, causing Playwright E2E smoke tests to fail with \ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS\.

## Affected file
\^Gpps/web/src/proxy.ts\ — lines 92–105

\\\	s
const isAppDomain = hostname.startsWith('app.');
const isApiDomain = hostname.startsWith('api.');
const isContentDomain = hostname.startsWith('content.');
const isPublicDomain = isContentDomain || (!isAppDomain && !isApiDomain);

// Public domain serves marketing content at the root.
if (isPublicDomain && pathname === '/') {
  return NextResponse.rewrite(new URL('/landing', request.url));
}
// Keep /landing as the canonical public landing route.
if (isPublicDomain && pathname === '/landing') {
  return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/', request.url));
}
\\\

## Fix
Treat \localhost\ and \127.0.0.1\ as app domains (not public domains) so CI/test traffic routes correctly. Options:
- Add \hostname === 'localhost' || hostname === '127.0.0.1'\ to the app-domain check
- Or treat \E2E_AUTH_BYPASS=1\ / \AUTH_BYPASS_USER=1\ as an implicit app-domain signal in the proxy

## Impact
- All E2E smoke and regression tests fail in CI on this PR and any future PR
- Blocks PR #260 from merging

## Steps to reproduce
Run \
ext start --hostname 127.0.0.1 --port 3010\ and navigate to \http://127.0.0.1:3010/\ in a browser or Playwright

